{# Greenfield purge for small HW (30G/50G).
   MUST run at position 0 of the HW template group: real 30G/50G ship with a
   factory `lan -> wan` firewall policy that registers `wan` as a policy
   dstintf, which collides with the sdwan-member datasrc validator. Purging
   the factory policy first is what lets `set interface "wan"` under
   `config system sdwan / config members` validate cleanly. (gotcha #23)
   Every stanza below is idempotent: safe on both fresh factory devices AND
   re-installs where the entries no longer exist. #}
config firewall policy
    purge
end
config system dhcp server
    purge
end
config firewall address
    edit "lan"
    next
    delete "lan"
end
config system virtual-switch
    purge
end
